cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HydroNet, please cite this software."
title: "HydroNet: A PyTorch Framework for Physics-Informed Deep Learning of the 2D Shallow Water Equations"
abstract: >-
  HydroNet is a PyTorch framework for solving the 2D shallow water equations (SWE)
  with physics-informed deep learning. It provides several model families that share
  a common Config/Dataset/Trainer pattern: a strong-form PINN (SWE_PINN), a
  physics-informed DeepONet operator surrogate (PI-SWE-DeepONet), and an FVM-PINN
  whose physics loss is a differentiable, well-balanced Roe finite-volume residual
  on unstructured SRH-2D meshes.
